# Pinned Aether toolchain versions for CI — the single place to bump.
#
# aeb tags are "later means later" markers, NOT semver promises; pin them so a
# CI run is reproducible. `ci/toolchain.sh` reads these; override at the shell to
# test a bump (e.g. `AETHER_REF=v0.591.0 ci/run.sh`).

# The Aether compiler (`ae`). Tag vX.Y.Z, branch, or commit SHA.
# Pinned to 0.643.0. The floor remains 0.638.0 — it carries the WebSocket client
# the BiDi work needs (std.http.ws_connect, first in 0.590 — see
# docs/WebDriver-BiDi.md) AND the single-file-module fix (aether aeec9b69 +
# a34ec231, "Accept single-file modules in [package] modules") that this repo's
# aether.toml [package] modules line depends on: `ae add
# github.com/aether-lang-dev/selaenium@<tag>` + `import webdriver` resolves with
# NO --lib only on >=0.638.0 (on 0.637.0 it was wrongly rejected as "does not
# exist"). 0.640-0.650 build the engine and all bindings clean, including the
# 6-platform cross-compiled jar matrix (verified on ae 0.650; aeb v0.299 pins
# 0.650 for its own build, and the ecosystem tracks it).
AETHER_REF=v0.650.0

# The aeb build runner. Tag v0.NNN, branch, or commit SHA.
# v0.300 standardizes the arch word on x86_64 (from amd64) across aeb — its
# release assets are now aeb-<os>-x86_64.tar.gz (with new -musl variants), and
# bldr._host_os_arch() emits <os>-x86_64. selaenium tracks that: ci/toolchain.sh
# fetches the x86_64 asset, the crossbuild lib names + jar /native/<os>-<arch>/
# paths use x86_64, and Native.osArch() emits x86_64 (still accepting the JVM's
# amd64 as input). v0.300 also carries the size() setter (v0.296), the copy-only
# bundle installer (v0.298), and bldr._host_arch/_host_os_arch. Verified: engine
# + 6-platform jar matrix + Java load build clean on aeb v0.300 / ae 0.650.
AEB_REF=v0.300
